  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to-be: completed/finished/ready-(e.g.-to-serve-or-eat) | very-drunk",
    "mnemonic": "You've seen the word <ja>出来る</ja> (to be able to do), which is the first part. Then the second part, <ja>上がる</ja> means \"to rise.\" So, think about it this way: once you're able to do something, you rise because you're finished. That's why this verb means <vocabulary>to be finished</vocabulary>.",
    "readingMnemonic": "The reading is a combination of the readings from <ja>出来る</ja> and <ja>上がる</ja>. So long as you were paying attention in lessons past, you should be able to read this word as well just by combining those other words.",
